To create a captivating website for Prospect Hero, I will develop a concrete build blueprint that incorporates a futuristic aesthetic direction, essential sections, and a responsive layout with interactive components.

```html
<!-- Index.html -->
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
    <title>Prospect Hero</title>
</head>
<body>
    <!-- Header Section -->
    <header>
        <nav>
            <ul>
                <li><a href="#home">Home</a></li>
                <li><a href="#gameplay">Gameplay</a></li>
                <li><a href="#features">Features</a></li>
            </ul>
        </nav>
    </header>

    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <section id="home">
        <h1>Prospect Hero</h1>
        <p>Embark on a thrilling adventure and become the ultimate hero.</p>
        <button>Play Now</button>
    </section>

    <!-- Gameplay Section -->
    <section id="gameplay">
        <h2>Gameplay Overview</h2>
        <p>Explore a vast open world, complete quests, and battle formidable enemies.</p>
        <img src="gameplay-image.jpg" alt="Gameplay Image">
    </section>

    <!-- Features Section -->
    <section id="features">
        <h2>Key Features</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Rich storyline with engaging characters</li>
            <li>Dynamic combat system with multiple skill trees</li>
            <li>Extensive character customization options</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Footer Section -->
    <footer>
        <p>&copy; 2024 Prospect Hero. All rights reserved.</p>
    </footer>

    <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>

<!-- styles.css -->
body {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
}

header {
    background-color: #333;
    color: #fff;
    padding: 1em;
    text-align: center;
}

header nav ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
}

header nav ul li {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-right: 20px;
}

header nav a {
    color: #fff;
    text-decoration: none;
}

#home {
    background-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, #333, #555);
    background-size: 100% 300px;
    background-position: 0% 100%;
    height: 100vh;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    color: #fff;
}

#gameplay {
    padding: 2em;
}

#features {
    padding: 2em;
}

footer {
    background-color: #333;
    color: #fff;
    padding: 1em;
    text-align: center;
    clear: both;
}

/* Add responsive design */
@media only screen and (max-width: 768px) {
    #home {
        height: 50vh;
    }

    #gameplay, #features {
        padding: 1em;
    }
}

/* Add interactive components */
#home button {
    background-color: #555;
    color: #fff;
    border: none;
    padding: 10px 20px;
    font-size: 16px;
    cursor: pointer;
}

#home button:hover {
    background-color: #666;
}

<!-- script.js -->
// Add event listener to the play now button
document.querySelector('button').addEventListener('click', () => {
    // Redirect to the game page or launch the game
    window.location.href = 'game.html';
});

// Add scroll event listener to the navigation menu
document.addEventListener('scroll', () => {
    const navbar = document.querySelector('header');
    if (window.scrollY > 50) {
        navbar.classList.add('scrolled');
    } else {
        navbar.classList.remove('scrolled');
    }
});
```

To run this code, you will need to install the following dependencies:
* No external dependencies are required, as this is a basic HTML, CSS, and JavaScript setup. However, you may want to consider using a package manager like npm to manage any additional libraries or frameworks you choose to use.

Stack:
- Frontend: HTML, CSS, JavaScript
- Backend: None (static website)
- Database: None (static website)

Pages:
- Index.html (home page)
- game.html (game page)

Data:
- Static data (game information, features, etc.)

Deploy Steps:
1. Create a new repository on a version control platform (e.g., GitHub).
2. Clone the repository to a local machine.
3. Create a new branch for the website (e.g., `website`).
4. Add the HTML, CSS, and JavaScript files to the repository.
5. Commit the changes and push them to the remote repository.
6. Set up a static website hosting service (e.g., GitHub Pages, Netlify).
7. Deploy the website to the hosting service.
8. Test the website for any issues or bugs.

